\f1\b \cf0 \
Action Import, Action Index & Action Link\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
Three folder action scripts to import, index or link to new files and folders. Use the script "Enable Folder Actions.scpt" to enable folder actions and afterwards the script "Attach Script to Folder.scpt" to attach the action scripts to one or more folders (those scripts are located in the folder /Library/Scripts). \ul Note:\ulnone  These scripts don't  require a specific location.\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 \
Finder Import\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
A toolbar script to import the contents of the folder of the active Finder window. Choose "Customize Toolbar..." (Mac-OS X 10.2 only) in the Finder and drop the script onto the toolbar. \ul Note:\ulnone  This script doesn't  require a specific location.\
\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Import selected Entourage messages\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural
\cf0 Imports all currently selected messages of Entourage as plain text. Copy the script to the folder "~/Documents/Microsoft User Data/\'caEntourage Script Menu Items". Afterwards it's possible to select this \'ca\'cascript from the Entourage Script Menu and imports the currently selected messages (DEVONthink is automatically launched).\
\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Import selected Eudora messages\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural
\cf0 Imports all currently selected messages of Eudora as plain text.\
\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Import selected mail\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
Imports all currently selected messages of Mail as plain text. Copy this script to the folder "~/Library/Scripts/Mail Scripts" and the script will be part of Mail's script menu afterwards. 
\f1\b \

\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Mail Import\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
Script to import all messages of all mailboxes of Mail as plain text. \ul Note: \ulnone This script doesn't require an installation - just start the script and the script will automatically launch Mail and DEVONthink afterwards.\
\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Save to DEVONthink\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
Copy this script to the folder "PDF Services" inside one of the Library directories. If there's no "PDF Services" folder, create one using the Finder.  But if there's an older version in this folder called "Save in DEVONthink", remove it. Afterwards the print panel of every application provides a new popup button to save the document in DEVONthink. \ul Note:\ulnone  This requires an installed printer to work properly and at least Mac-OS X 10.2.4! \
\
\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Copy from Safari to DEVONthink\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
A QuicKey macro by Kee Hinckley which copies the selected text from Safari to DEVONthink and inserts the URL of the page too. The default key for this shortcut is Cmd-Ctrl-C.\
\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Copy from Eudora to DEVONthink\
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\slleading40\ql\qnatural

\f0\b0 \cf0 \
A QuicKey macro by Kee Hinckley which copies the selected email from Eudora to DEVONthink and sets the title of the new document to the summary line (this requires viewing your messages in a pane instead of a different window). The default key for this shortcut is Cmd-Ctrl-C.\
\
\ul Notes:\ulnone  \
\pard\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx5760\tx7200\li140\fi-140\slleading40\ql\qnatural
\cf0 - These two macros require the shareware QuicKeys X2 available at www.quickeys.com/downloads.html. Use "File > Import Shortcuts" to import them and switch the scope of the "QuicKeys Editor" window to "All Shortcuts" to view, enable, disable or edit them.\
\
- You can use the same shortcut for both macros if the scopes of the macros are limited to Safari and Eudora only (this is the default setting).}